# nosemgrep: package_managers.npm.npm-missing-minimum-release-age.npm-missing-minimum-release-age
# (min-release-age is an npm 11.10 setting; this repo installs with pnpm 9, which
# does not read it. Release-age gating is Renovate's minimumReleaseAge: 7 days and
# installs run with --frozen-lockfile, so nothing new resolves outside a reviewed PR.)
# The package publishes to (and consumers install from) GitHub Packages.
# Only the scope -> registry mapping is committed. Auth is supplied outside the
# repo: semantic-release uses NPM_TOKEN to publish; anyone INSTALLING published
# versions adds `//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=<token with read:packages>`
# to their user-level ~/.npmrc (developing this repo needs no token at all).
@datagriff:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
